12→ * Tracks departed nodes and manages the grace period before permanent removal.
13→ *
14→ * <p>
15→ * Contract: Records node departures with timestamps. A departed node is considered in
16→ * grace period if the configured duration has not elapsed since departure. After grace
17→ * period expiry, the departure is permanent. If a node returns during grace, its
18→ * departure record is cleared. Grace period controls cleanup timing, not ownership
19→ * assignment — partitions are eagerly reassigned on departure.
20→ *
21→ * <p>
22→ * Thread-safe: uses concurrent data structures.
23→ *
24→ * <p>
25→ * Governed by: {@code .decisions/rebalancing-grace-period-strategy/adr.md}
26→ */
27→public final class GracePeriodManager {
28→
29→    private final Duration gracePeriod;
30→    private final ConcurrentHashMap<NodeAddress, Instant> departures = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
31→
32→    /**
33→     * Creates a grace period manager with the specified duration.
34→     *
35→     * @param gracePeriod the grace period duration; must not be null and must be positive
36→     */
37→    public GracePeriodManager(Duration gracePeriod) {
38→        Objects.requireNonNull(gracePeriod, "gracePeriod must not be null");
39→        if (gracePeriod.isNegative() || gracePeriod.isZero()) {
40→            throw new IllegalArgumentException("gracePeriod must be positive");
41→        }
42→        this.gracePeriod = gracePeriod;
43→    }
